// 14758
[enum_14758]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> The day we moved here, Primrose was two. I remember her toddling next to us, carrying a book, one of the bigger ones.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> You couldn't stop her. We called her our little Pack Yak Primrose.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Sure, she slowed us down, made the journey painfully long, but you try to tell her to stop!
val=3,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Ah. Good days.
default=null

// 14759
[enum_14759]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=310>The day we moved here, Primrose was two. I remember her toddling next to us, carrying a book, one of the bigger ones.
val=1,<p=310>You couldn't stop her. We called her our little Pack Yak Primrose.
val=2,<p=310>Sure, she slowed us down, made the journey painfully long, but you try to tell her to stop!
val=3,<p=310>Ah. Good days.
default=null

// 14760
[enum_14760]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> You can ignore death, blood, murder. The mind's flexible like that. They all happen to far away people with far away lives.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> It was blissful. We lived in a house where those things didn't exist.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> But it was like we were pulling back the curtains and hoping for the best. Hoping that those flimsy pieces of fabric would keep the violence out.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> We were wrong. The world got in. A sea troll got in...
default=null

// 14761
[enum_14761]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=2>You can ignore death, blood, murder. The mind's flexible like that. They all happen to far away people with far away lives.
val=1,<p=2>It was blissful. We lived in a house where those things didn't exist.
val=2,<p=2>But it was like we were pulling back the curtains and hoping for the best. Hoping that those flimsy pieces of fabric would keep the violence out.
val=3,<p=0>We were wrong. The world got in. A sea troll got in...
default=null

// 14762
[enum_14762]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Gail didn't come to us at first. She'd been watching us for some time from the Needle, making sure we weren't monsters, I guess.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> I mean, we'd seen her. She wasn't great at hiding herself, after all. She's ten-foot tall and blue.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Joss assumed the worst, as he always did. Tried to scare her away with air blasts. Nothing that would hurt her, just to send a message.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> She kept clear. It was only when Joss left - no, abandoned - us that she felt courage enough to talk to me.
default=null

// 14763
[enum_14763]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=2>Gail didn't come to us at first. She'd been watching us for some time from the Needle, making sure we weren't monsters, I guess.
val=1,<p=2>I mean, we'd seen her. She wasn't great at hiding herself, after all. She's ten-foot tall and blue.
val=2,<p=2>Joss assumed the worst, as he always did. Tried to scare her away with air blasts. Nothing that would hurt her, just to send a message.
val=3,<p=2>She kept clear. It was only when Joss left - no, abandoned - us that she felt courage enough to talk to me.
default=null

// 14764
[enum_14764]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Primrose is so strong, but people can't see past the illness.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Doctors, visitors, they all make that mistake. Judge her by the disease, the microscopic evil magnified into something huge.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> But I see the strength. Damn girl never lets an argument go un-won. She'll fight for the things she loves, for sure.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> And she's full of love. Not always for her mum, but, you know, it's there. Growing up, she loved everything, cared for everything.
default=null

// 14765
[enum_14765]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=300>Primrose is so strong, but people can't see past the illness.
val=1,<p=300>Doctors, visitors, they all make that mistake. Judge her by the disease, the microscopic evil magnified into something huge.
val=2,<p=310>But I see the strength. Damn girl never lets an argument go un-won. She'll fight for the things she loves, for sure.
val=3,<p=310>And she's full of love. Not always for her mum, but, you know, it's there. Growing up, she loved everything, cared for everything.
default=null

// 14766
[enum_14766]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> My whole life, I've been surrounded by books. Not once have I read one.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> I can see my tombstone: 'crushed under a pile of books'.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> When I met Joss, he was hidden behind a stack of wizarding tomes. He'd line our house with them.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Primrose treated them as toys, then things to climb, then adventures to climb into.
val=4,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Her imagination was always wild. She'd play out the God Wars with Saradomin as a ladle and Zamorak as a pepper pot.
default=null

// 14767
[enum_14767]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=2>My whole life, I've been surrounded by books. Not once have I read one.
val=1,<p=315>I can see my tombstone: 'crushed under a pile of books'.
