val=3,<p=2>Primrose treated them as toys, then things to climb, then adventures to climb into.
val=4,<p=2>Her imagination was always wild. She'd play out the God Wars with Saradomin as a ladle and Zamorak as a pepper pot.
default=null

// 14768
[enum_14768]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Every weekend, it was the same thing. Pack provisions, wrap some books in blessed cloth and worry about leaving Primrose behind.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Then it was the trip to the Wizard's Tower, cart and all. Sell some books to Sloop, ask around about Joss, cook a Weekend Banquet for the elite wizards.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Then it was back home, worried about Primrose and whether Gail had kept her safe.
default=null

// 14769
[enum_14769]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=2>Every weekend, it was the same thing. Pack provisions, wrap some books in blessed cloth and worry about leaving Primrose behind.
val=1,<p=2>Then it was the trip to the Wizard's Tower, cart and all. Sell some books to Sloop, ask around about Joss, cook a Weekend Banquet for the elite wizards.
val=2,<p=2>Then it was back home, worried about Primrose and whether Gail had kept her safe.
default=null

// 14770
[enum_14770]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Some memories stick in you like barbs. They hurt whenever you accidentally catch yourself on them.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> I...I was on the way back from the Wizard's Tower. The day had gone well: I'd sold some books for more than I expected, and I'd gotten the cooking job.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> But I arrived at the house. There was the bang-bang of the door, slamming in the wind.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> I abandoned the cart, rushed in. I called for Primrose. Nothing.
val=4,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> A stray sea troll had found its way into the house. It was long gone when I got there, but... It...
val=5,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> It had killed her. Primrose.
val=6,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> That was the first time Gail talked to me. I couldn't move, I was crying on the floor of the kitchen. And Gail came to me.
default=null

// 14771
[enum_14771]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=309>Some memories stick in you like barbs. They hurt whenever you accidentally catch yourself on them.
val=1,<p=2>I...I was on the way back from the Wizard's Tower. The day had gone well: I'd sold some books for more than I expected, and I'd gotten the cooking job.
val=2,<p=302>But I arrived at the house. There was the bang-bang of the door, slamming in the wind.
val=3,<p=302>I abandoned the cart, rushed in. I called for Primrose. Nothing.
val=4,<p=302>A stray sea troll had found its way into the house. It was long gone when I got there, but... It...
val=5,<p=309>It had killed her. Primrose.
val=6,<p=309>That was the first time Gail talked to me. I couldn't move, I was crying on the floor of the kitchen. And Gail came to me.
default=null

// 14772
[enum_14772]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> 'Temper-temper'. That's what Joss would always say to me. Gods, it would only make me angrier.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Whenever I would hook his nose out of a damned book: 'temper-temper'.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Whenever I called him on his laziness, doing the chores with some cheap magic: 'temper-temper'.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> They were even his last words to me before he left. Wherever the bastard has gone, I imagine him repeating them like a cheap toy.
default=null

// 14773
[enum_14773]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=300>'Temper-temper'. That's what Joss would always say to me. Gods, it would only make me angrier.
val=1,<p=300>Whenever I would hook his nose out of a damned book: 'temper-temper'.
val=2,<p=300>Whenever I called him on his laziness, doing the chores with some cheap magic: 'temper-temper'.
val=3,<p=300>They were even his last words to me before he left. Wherever the bastard has gone, I imagine him repeating them like a cheap toy.
default=null

// 14774
[enum_14774]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> A year to live. That's all the doctor could give her, holding his hands out upright like a pauper. 'Please miss, this is all I can give you'.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Primrose just half-smiled when the doctor told her. I was so angry at her for brushing it all aside.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> I needed her to cry, break down, something. Just react, damn it!
val=3,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> *sighs*
val=4,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Each month, I watched helplessly as she got thinner. Her skin became translucent. But you know Primrose: it just meant that her character shone through brighter.
val=5,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> I just wish...I wish she didn't hide that character away. So often, she reserved it for her creatures. Her monsters.
default=null

// 14775
[enum_14775]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=300>A year to live. That's all the doctor could give her, holding his hands out upright like a pauper. 'Please miss, this is all I can give you'.
val=1,<p=300>Primrose just half-smiled when the doctor told her. I was so angry at her for brushing it all aside.
val=2,<p=300>I needed her to cry, break down, something. Just react, damn it!
val=3,<p=0>*sighs*
val=4,<p=0>Each month, I watched helplessly as she got thinner. Her skin became translucent. But you know Primrose: it just meant that her character shone through brighter.
val=5,<p=0>I just wish...I wish she didn't hide that character away. So often, she reserved it for her creatures. Her monsters.
default=null

// 14776
[enum_14776]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> When I was younger, I'd fall in love twice a week. It would come to me as easy as a temper, and would disappear just as quick.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> I thought I would fall out of love with Joss as quickly as the others. In the end, the love went, but it took a while.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> There was my love for Saradomin, of course. But I wasn't getting love in return. The score wasn't equal.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Primrose has always been the exception. To fall out of love with Primrose would be to fall out of love with, well, everything.
val=4,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> I know what you're thinking. No - that time doesn't count. I wasn't angry with Primrose. I was angry at THEM.
default=null

// 14777
[enum_14777]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=310>When I was younger, I'd fall in love twice a week. It would come to me as easy as a temper, and would disappear just as quick.
val=1,<p=2>I thought I would fall out of love with Joss as quickly as the others. In the end, the love went, but it took a while.
val=2,<p=2>There was my love for Saradomin, of course. But I wasn't getting love in return. The score wasn't equal.
val=3,<p=310>Primrose has always been the exception. To fall out of love with Primrose would be to fall out of love with, well, everything.
val=4,<p=300>I know what you're thinking. No - that time doesn't count. I wasn't angry with Primrose. I was angry at THEM.
default=null

// 14778
[enum_14778]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> There was a day when the illness hit her hard. A day when she couldn't ignore it.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> Primrose dropped her favourite book: the Adventures of Hannibus, I think it was. She couldn't pick it up. It was open on its back page, the ending staring right up at her.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Megan:</col> It was the first time I'd seen her cry since the illness. I tried to hand it to her, but she shoved it away. I felt like her jailer.
default=null

// 14779
