// 14842
[enum_14842]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> There's a story in one of the books. It was the only one mum liked to read to me.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> It's about a giant, Dubbo, who keeps a flock of sheep. He loves those sheep: force-feeds them hay; throws them from hand to hand to make sure they wake up;
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> taps them on the head with his club, to make sure they go to sleep.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Each day, one runs away. He can't understand why - he treats them so well! So, he eats that runaway sheep - in one go, pop! - to send a message to the others.
val=4,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> But they keep running away, and he keeps eating them, pop pop pop! Eventually, only one remains.
val=5,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> That sheep, Baba, puts up with the feeding, the throwing, the taps on the head. Does nothing. And Dubbo sits down in front of that sheep.
val=6,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> 'What's wrong with you, little runt?', the giant asks. But Baba won't answer, and won't run away.
val=7,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> 'Why won't you run away?', said Dubbo. He didn't know it, but he wanted the sheep to run away. 
val=8,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> So he goes out, gets into a fight with another giant and gets eaten himself. It's an odd story.
val=9,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Still, I like having Baba around the house as one of my friends. She visits and we chat. She's a real gossip, you know?
default=null

// 14843
[enum_14843]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>There's a story in one of the books. It was the only one mum liked to read to me.
val=1,<p=0>It's about a giant, Dubbo, who keeps a flock of sheep. He loves those sheep: force-feeds them hay; throws them from hand to hand to make sure they wake up; taps them on the head with his club, to make sure they go to sleep.
val=2,<p=0>Each day, one runs away. He can't understand why - he treats them so well! So, he eats that runaway sheep - in one go, pop! - to send a message to the others.
val=3,<p=0>But they keep running away, and he keeps eating them, pop pop pop! Eventually, only one remains.
val=4,<p=0>That sheep, Baba, puts up with the feeding, the throwing, the taps on the head. Does nothing. And Dubbo sits down in front of that sheep.
val=5,<p=0>'What's wrong with you, little runt?', the giant asks. But Baba won't answer, and won't run away.
val=6,<p=0>'Why won't you run away?', said Dubbo. He didn't know it, but he wanted the sheep to run away. 
val=7,<p=0>So he goes out, gets into a fight with another giant and gets eaten himself. It's an odd story.
val=8,<p=0>Still, I like having Baba around the house as one of my friends. She visits and we chat. She's a real gossip, you know?
default=null

// 14844
[enum_14844]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> She mentioned it! I didn't even bring it up.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> She said the scar was from a wizard at the Wizards' Tower, an accident, and she didn't feel safe going back. From now on, she's staying at home.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> It's a big old bag of lies. It stinks. Not once did she look me in the eye. Gah! She's such an awful liar! 
val=3,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> It crossed my mind that the scar was just an excuse to stop going to the Tower. Did she know about Sloop? Was this all to stop us talking to each other through the books?
val=4,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Oh, Sloop, what am I going to do now?
default=null

// 14845
[enum_14845]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>She mentioned it! I didn't even bring it up.
val=1,<p=0>She said the scar was from a wizard at the Wizards' Tower, an accident, and she didn't feel safe going back. From now on, she's staying at home.
val=2,<p=0>It's a big old bag of lies. It stinks. Not once did she look me in the eye. Gah! She's such an awful liar! 
val=3,<p=0>It crossed my mind that the scar was just an excuse to stop going to the Tower. Did she know about Sloop? Was this all to stop us talking to each other through the books?
val=4,<p=0>Oh, Sloop, what am I going to do now?
default=null

// 14846
[enum_14846]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> I've never really had a problem with being bored. I read, I write. And there's always my friends.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> My friends were a gift from my dad. A little apology before the utter scumbag ran away. When I read a book, the character pops into existence. But no one else can see them.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Some of them I don't care much for. I've learned to keep them locked in their books. But Thok, and the others - I couldn't be without them.
default=null

// 14847
[enum_14847]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>I've never really had a problem with being bored. I read, I write. And there's always my friends.
val=1,<p=0>My friends were a gift from my dad. A little apology before the utter scumbag ran away. When I read a book, the character pops into existence. But no one else can see them.
val=2,<p=0>Some of them I don't care much for. I've learned to keep them locked in their books. But Thok, and the others - I couldn't be without them.
default=null

// 14848
[enum_14848]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Doing anything for more than a few minutes is the ultimate pain in the backside. My lungs burn, my knees go to jelly. I just fall over and want to go to sleep.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Mum used to get medicines. It took all of our money to do it, but I wasn't going to convince her to stop. Megan's the only one who changes Megan's mind. 
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> The medicines would let me leave the bed, for a few days at least. And it would bring a smile to my mum! Then I'd be back to bed like a brick fell on me.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> I had the idea of stealing some of the medicine for myself. You know, when mum wasn't there. But she rationed it so carefully! 
val=4,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> And we can't afford it now, anyway. Not now mum's given up the job at the Wizards' Tower.
